Expected/actual mismatch from earlier same-commit host smoke: earlier output reported POST proxy 502 `fetch failed` while direct POST was 201. The current correctly configured Compose run did not reproduce it (proxy POST 201). Earlier evidence also had an inconsistent Next request line showing 201. Root cause remains undetermined; no implementation attribution or owner is assigned.
Payment status route probe: GET /payments/<valid-shaped UUID>/status returned 404 both direct and through proxy. Probe omitted Authorization only to detect route registration. Static implementation inventory found no GET status handler. This is not proof that the Contract's authenticated missing-payment 404 behavior is implemented.
Minimal status-route reproduction (commit fb293e2ac35c0fe29fbe3573bf5edf81b7a586a0): GET /payments/<valid-shaped UUID>/status direct to backend and GET /api/backend/payments/<valid-shaped UUID>/status through Next, with no Authorization header. API Contract v4.0 §5 expects the protected route to be registered (401 without JWT; with valid owner JWT, 200 for owned payment, 400 for invalid UUID and 404 for absent/foreign payment). Actual: 404 direct and proxied. Because no route/controller exists, authenticated owner/foreign-owner behavior was not testable; this is an implementation gap relative to Contract, not proof of the Contract's 404 ownership behavior. No JWT or real UUID logged.
This is an API/HTTP smoke, not a real browser screenshot or VNPay Sandbox E2E.
